--- body ---
## Context

The author ruled 2026-08-31 that seg/1 is for **books and proceedings first**
and that the dictionary is a rare case. Every clause of `spec/DESIGN.md` §2.2's
segmenter was written for the dictionary, so the rare case had been standing in
for the common one and the spec now says the wrong thing in four places.

This ticket is the propagation only. The ruling is in `spec/DECISIONS.md` and is
not restated here beyond what the edits need.

## The sites, and what each becomes

1. **`spec/DESIGN.md` §2.2, the heuristic list.** The headword *rhythm* — median
   gap and MAD over candidate spacing — is a uniformity statistic and books and
   proceedings are not uniform. It is demoted from core signal to the rare
   class's special case. What takes its place as the primary signal set: a table
   of contents to validate the cut set against rather than only score it,
   chapter and section numbering, author bylines (no dictionary analogue, and
   the strongest single signal in a proceedings), and chapter starts on page
   boundaries — form feeds, present in the newer extractor generation only per
   ticket 0120, so exploited where present and never required.
2. **`spec/DESIGN.md` §2.2, the entry arithmetic.** The "first-class peers"
   paragraph is the dictionary's arithmetic and calls itself the entry ruling's
   whole point. It becomes the illustration: a book's entry is a chapter, tens
   per item rather than hundreds. Check whether §2.9's passage estimate moves —
   total text is unchanged, so passage counts should not, but entry *collapse*
   behaviour does, since fewer and larger entries mean fewer hits per item.
3. **`spec/DESIGN.md` §2.2, the fallback.** Synthetic entries of ~6k tokens
   approximate a dictionary entry and are a fraction of a book chapter, so a
   book below the confidence gate is shredded into fragments that are neither
   entries nor chapters. Re-size against the primary class or state why it holds.
4. **X5's rule (`spec/DESIGN.md` §3, ticket 0025) and `spec/DESIGN.md` §5 risk 1.**
   Corpus and ground truth both change, and this is where the ruling makes the
   work *cheaper*: hand-scoring 50 cuts against a printed dictionary needed a
   human with the physical book, where a book's own table of contents is
   mechanical ground truth for the cut set seg/1 should have produced. The bar's
   form survives; what it is sampled from does not, and whether ≥ 45/50 is still
   the right number against easier ground truth is a question for the author,
   not a number to carry over silently.
5. **Ticket 0028's exit criteria**, which name the dictionary as the thing seg/1
   runs over.

## What must NOT move

The dictionary holds a second, unrelated role: the monster document.
`spec/REQUIREMENTS.md` makes a 15 000-page PDF first-class, X3a baselines the
uncapped document at the 2 084,9 MiB class, and §2.8's RSS gate is calibrated
against it. Demoting the dictionary as a segmenter TARGET leaves it exactly
where it is as an RSS FIXTURE. `spec/DESIGN.md` §1's extraction-cap example is
likewise a coverage statement, not a segmenter one. Two roles, one document;
only the first moves — a propagation that greps for the document and edits every
hit takes the fixture with it.

## Exit criteria

- [x] §2.2's heuristics rewritten for the primary class, the rhythm statistic
      kept as the rare case's special case rather than deleted
      (SPEC.md 5.2.2; the glossary entry at SPEC.md 3 repointed with it)
- [x] the entry arithmetic reframed, and §2.9 checked rather than assumed
      (SPEC.md 5.2.9's 567 829 is measured over total text and does not move;
      what moves is entry collapse, and 5.2.2 now says so)
- [x] the synthetic fallback re-sized against a chapter, or its size defended
      (ruled 2026-09-02, DECISIONS.md: one constant, ~12k tokens, for every
      class; the ~6k figure retired, the deferral to X5 deleted since X5
      samples accepted boundaries and cannot measure a fallback)
- [x] X5's corpus and ground truth restated in §3 and ticket 0025, with the
      bar's number put to the author rather than carried over
      (ruled 2026-09-02, DECISIONS.md: ground truth is the embedded outline
      with the outline tier held out, both paths measured, 50 cuts per class
      at 45/50, verdicts never pooled, primary and dictionary arms gating;
      SPEC.md 5.2.2 gained the PDF path's paragraph so 5.3 can name its tier)
- [x] 0028's exit criteria repointed
- [x] the RSS-fixture sites verified untouched, by name: §1, §2.8, X3a, R-scale
      (no removed line in the diff names the 2 084,9 MiB class, the 15 000-page
      PDF, the RSS gate or X3a)
